course: dictionary
lesson: 2337
title: Crumple: creased, collapsed, crushed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To crumple something is to squeeze it so it gets full of creases, like a piece of paper screwed up in your fist. «Dad had to iron Mia's crumpled shirt before the party.» Crumpled means creased, not torn. Check by swapping in your meaning: a creased shirt still makes sense in the sentence.
explain: The same word can describe a body falling. To crumple can mean to fall down suddenly in a heap, folding up like paper. Nothing has to be squeezed by hands here. Look at the clues around the word, such as falling, heap or ground, to find the meaning.
explain: Engineers use crumple on purpose. «Modern cars are built to protect the people inside: the front of the car crumples on purpose to slow everyone more gently.» A crumple zone is a part of a car that squashes in a crash, so the stop takes a little longer and the force on people is smaller. Here crumple means to be crushed in a controlled way.
explain: Crumple can also describe a face. When someone is about to cry, their face creases up and folds in. Words like sad, tears or about to cry around the word are your clues. Always ask: what fits here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Crumple means to squeeze something so it gets creases, or to fall down suddenly in a heap.
fact: «Crumpled» means full of creases, as in «a crumpled shirt».
fact: A «crumple zone» is a part of a car that squashes in a crash to protect the people inside.
fact: When a face crumples, it creases up, often just before someone cries.
fact: A check you can always use: swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Dad had to iron the crumpled shirt before the party.» What does crumpled mean here? | *Full of creases | Clean and newly washed | Bright red | Torn into small pieces
exercise: «The front of the car crumples on purpose in a crash.» What is a crumple zone for? | Keeping the car dry in the rain | Making the car look nicer | *Making the stop longer and softer, so the force on people is smaller | Making the car go faster
exercise: «A new butterfly pumps fluid into its crumpled wings until they open.» What does crumpled wings mean here? | *Wings folded and creased, not yet open | Wings that have flown far away | Wings that are very bright | Wings made of paper
test: What does crumple mean when a face does it? | To turn bright red | *To crease up, as if about to cry | To grow longer | To smile widely
test: What is a crumple zone? | A flat tyre | *A part of a car built to squash in a crash and protect people | A window that opens | A seat that folds down
exam: Which of these best matches crumple? | Fold neatly into a square | *Squeeze into creases | Stretch out flat | Carry something heavy
